              },
              "value": "Bulk gauge algebra is GSM; Q,U,D,L,E are bulk fermions with three generations (Yukawas3x3) and one bulk complex Higgs doublet. Odd-dimensional fermions are vector-like bulk spinors, NOT 4D Weyl fields. Source zero modes U,D,E are RH, but five-dimensional bulk representations retain source colour3,Y=2/3,-1/3,-1; no blind 4D conjugation."
            },
            {
              "id": "five",
              "basis": "source_statement",
              "locator": {
                "section_equations": "Section2 Eqs.(2.2)-(2.3), explicit delta=1 reduction",
                "pdf_pages": [
                  5
                ],
                "anchor": "For δ = 1, the KK decomposition"
              },
              "value": "Source explicitly defines delta=1 on S1/Z2. Encode Lorentz B2 [0,1] for each bulk spinor and [0,0] for scalar. KK levels/gauge fifth components are modes of bulk fields, not extra elementary inventory copies. Generic delta family remains distinct; even-dimensional singlet anomaly completions not fixed."
            },
            {
              "id": "baseline",
              "basis": "declared_atlas_baseline",
              "locator": {
                "file": "atlas/FIELD_CONTENT_CONVENTIONS.md",
                "section": "explicit F_SM/R_SM/R_MSSM templates"
              },
              "value": "Source-explicit SM/MSSM inheritance is expanded using the declared atlas baseline: three ordinary SM chiral families, no independent RH neutrino unless stated. Exact Dynkin and all-LH conversion are conventions/derivations, not newly printed source tables. Gauge connections and dependent conjugates are not extra matter."
            }
          ],
          "derivation": "Exact highest weights use dynkin-gauge-1. prepare_entry expands identified 4D Dirac/RH fermions into LH conjugates of every factor, and applies one primitive positive charge unit over the entire inventory. Retain source-coordinate row above; scalar-realification equivalence is NOT implemented."
